    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0542" n="1296" xml:id="pg1296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Sp1/32</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-22T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 23, 6.50
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>836. Department’s 718, October 20, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d450-f1"/> Spanish
                    Government has of its own accord taken action suggested by Department. Officers
                    and crew of German submarine <hi rendition="#italic">B–23</hi> which entered
                    Corunna in July have just been sent to Alcala de Henares, a few miles from
                    Madrid for internment. Submarine remains under Spanish surveillance at
                    Ferrol.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
